# Secrets harvest output - contains LIVE credentials for third parties.
# Kept on disk for the owner's inspection, deliberately NOT committed.
SECRETS.txt

# The development database credentials. Never committed, never in a script.
.env.development

# The decompiled original application.
#
# It is another party's source code. The ANALYSIS of it (docs/reverse-engineering/) is
# published, because that is the valuable part and it is our own work. The decompiled
# source is kept locally as the evidence behind the analysis, and it is not published.
#
# If this project is republished and the owner holds the rights to the original, remove
# these two lines and run `git add -f reference/decompiled` to include it.
reference/decompiled/
reference/decompiled.tar.gz

